# Self-improvement loop

After substantive work, look for missing guidance before ending.

## Encode trigger

Update a skill or rule when **any** of these are true:

- The user corrected the same class of mistake twice in one session
- A lint or `pnpm garden:health` failure recurred after you thought it was fixed
- You improvised a convention that should be standard (voice, wikilinks, deploy, ponytail)

## Where to write it

| Domain | Target |
|--------|--------|
| Notes garden voice/shape | `.cursor/skills/garden-voice/SKILL.md` or `anti-slop.mdc` |
| Blog voice | `.cursor/skills/jorap-voice/SKILL.md` |
| Flashcards | `.cursor/skills/flashcards/SKILL.md` |
| Hugo/theme | `.cursor/skills/hugo-template-guidance/SKILL.md` |
| Repo tooling / deploy | `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` or `package.json` scripts |
| Intentional shortcut | `ponytail:` comment in code → `/ponytail-debt` |

One line per lesson. Delete obsolete guidance when you add the new line.

## Do not encode

- One-off typos, one-time user preferences, or content facts that belong in notes under `content/`
- Speculative rules for problems that have not happened yet (YAGNI)

## Pair with maintenance

Weekly: `pnpm garden:health` (see `garden-maintenance` skill). Monthly: `/ponytail-debt` on `ponytail:` markers.
